SUMMARY:Brass Bed
LOCATION:Blue Moon Saloon and Guest House\, 215 East Convent Street\, Lafay
 ette
DESCRIPTION:Brass Bed\n\nEmerging from Lafayette\, Louisiana\, Brass Bed ha
 s spent years carving out a distinctive place in the independent music sce
 ne with a sound that blends psychedelic rock\, power pop\, indie rock\, an
 d adventurous songwriting.\n\nFormed in 2004\, the band built a reputation
  for crafting catchy melodies wrapped in swirling guitars\, analog synthes
 izers\, fuzz\, and expansive psychedelic textures. Drawing inspiration fro
 m artists like The Beatles\, The Beach Boys\, Big Star\, and classic alter
 native rock\, Brass Bed balances infectious pop sensibilities with an unpr
 edictable\, experimental edge.\n\nThe band earned critical acclaim with al
 bums including Melt White (2010)\, The Secret Will Keep You (2013)\, and I
 n the Yellow Leaf (2016). Their music has taken them beyond Louisiana\, in
 cluding a memorable appearance on NPR's Tiny Desk Concert series.\n\nFeatu
 ring longtime members Jonny Campos\, Peter DeHart\, and Christiaan Mader\,
  Brass Bed returned with new music in 2025\, bringing fresh energy and sha
 rper songwriting to their signature sound.\n\nWith deep roots in Acadiana 
 and a sound that reaches far beyond regional boundaries\, Brass Bed delive
 rs a live experience full of shimmering melodies\, gritty guitars\, psyche
 delic exploration\, and good old-fashioned rock and roll.\n\nhttps://event
 s.timely.fun/kw4jncf1/event/78485759/20261128210000
